Counts the words in a text, given as a string literal.
A word is a run of characters that are not spaces (code 32).
The probe is text processing: a string is a list of bytes, and the program walks it with a state that says whether it is inside a word.
---
---
(lam s
  (letrec go (lam l (lam inword (lam count
      (if (? l)
          count
          (let c (head l)
            (let space (= c 32)
              (go (tail l) (if space 0 1) (+ count (if space 0 (if inword 0 1))))))))))
    (go s 0 0)))
---
"" => 0 fuel 200000
"hello" => 1 fuel 200000
"hello world" => 2 fuel 200000
"  a  b c " => 3 fuel 200000
"one two three four" => 4 fuel 200000
